 A numerical simulation analysis.

In the study presented hereby, an ocean engineering project simuated a situation about
how big is water flow at stone pillar of the coastal pier? By running this experiment using 6 meters and wave 12, in total there are nine models.

For our project the data will look more specific as:
Wave period of about 12 s
Wave heights up-to (2 meter )
wave energy
Water currents in a specific point near or on a fixed location

A numerical experiment can then be implemented on such
parameters. So it looks how different wave energies effect water velocity.
Wave direction 180 degree
Depth around that pillar should be around about a maximum level. (1m)


This project uses computational software OpenSource called SWATH.

We want also use python scripts (and) SWATH as our primary computational resource,
also will we compare this outcome by comparing with real-life experiment results from
the site near-by.


This research paper can explore on these factors like 
* Effects from a wave with direction.
   wave with direction (or without any)

Wave with high speed,
and
without high Speed


For future references: This information might provide us information in designing for
a pier to handle wave effects or water quality issues.

Our hypothesis would is "As an energy increases the water currents increase"
And our research objective for us: We hope find more detail to understand wave
behavior near and around fixed structures.
The data of real life observations is compared with the simulation.

Data of this data set was measured over
12 s wave cycles.
we compare and check if these values can predict wave direction
or we see any changes or correlations to our model in SWAth.



